1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,860
Chapter one, the pain, a sharp tearing sensation ripped through June's lower abdomen.

2
00:00:05,259 --> 00:00:09,199
It was so sudden, so violently intense that her fingers went numb.

3
00:00:09,599 --> 00:00:11,500
The glass of water slipped from her hand.

4
00:00:11,759 --> 00:00:15,279
It hit the hardwood floor, shattering into dozens of jagged pieces.

5
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:20,199
The sound echoed loudly in the massive empty master bedroom of the Compton estate.

6
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:23,320
June tried to take a step forward, but her knees buckled.

7
00:00:23,519 --> 00:00:27,839
A cold sweat instantly broke out across her forehead, sticking her hair to her skin.

8
00:00:27,839 --> 00:00:32,439
She collapsed onto the expensive Persian rug, her hands flying to her stomach.

9
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:34,840
Her lungs forgot how to pull in air.

10
00:00:35,119 --> 00:00:36,719
The pain wasn't just a dull ache.

11
00:00:36,979 --> 00:00:39,920
It felt like a serrated blade twisting inside her organs.

12
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:42,740
Her vision blurred at the edges, turning gray.

13
00:00:43,079 --> 00:00:43,979
She knew her body.

14
00:00:44,259 --> 00:00:45,759
She was a medical researcher.

15
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,140
This was not a normal pregnancy cramp.

16
00:00:48,359 --> 00:00:49,740
Her vital signs were crashing.

17
00:00:50,159 --> 00:00:52,500
Her phone was on the nightstand, three feet away.

18
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:55,100
It looked like a mile, trembling violently.

19
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:57,539
June dragged her body across the floor.

20
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:00,740
The jagged pieces of the broken glass bid into her knee,

21
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:03,659
but she couldn't even feel it over the agony in her abdomen.

22
00:01:04,079 --> 00:01:08,719
She reached up, her fingers blindly clawing at the nightstand until she knocked the phone down.

23
00:01:09,079 --> 00:01:10,819
The bright screen pierced her eyes.

24
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:13,079
Her fingers were slick with cold sweat.

25
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:14,719
She pressed the speed dial.

26
00:01:15,219 --> 00:01:16,060
Number one, coal.

27
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:17,340
The phone rang once.

28
00:01:17,780 --> 00:01:19,239
June squeezed her eyes shut.

29
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:23,579
Her fingernails digging so hard into her palms that the skin broke please.

30
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:24,260
Please.

31
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:25,939
It rang a second time.

32
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:29,180
Each second stretched out heavy and suffocating.

33
00:01:29,659 --> 00:01:30,540
Then a click.

34
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:31,280
What?

35
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:33,099
Cole's voice came through the speaker.

36
00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:34,319
It wasn't a greeting.

37
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:35,760
It was a wall of ice.

38
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:39,540
In the background, June could hear the clinking of champagne flutes

39
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:41,739
and the smooth jazz of a live band.

40
00:01:42,159 --> 00:01:43,299
Cole, June gasped.

41
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:44,599
Her throat tight and dry.

42
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,019
Help me, the baby.

43
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:50,620
Before Cole could respond, a high-pitched sweet voice drifted through the receiver.

44
00:01:50,959 --> 00:01:52,000
Cole, who is it?

45
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,719
We're going to be late for the red carpet.

46
00:01:53,719 --> 00:01:54,359
Alicia.

47
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,420
June's stomach lurched.

48
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:59,400
The pain spiked, sending a wave of nausea up her throat.

49
00:01:59,819 --> 00:02:00,840
June, Cole said.

50
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:03,980
His tone dropping into a low, impatient growl.

51
00:02:04,219 --> 00:02:07,519
If this is your pathetic attempt to stop me from attending the gala,

52
00:02:07,799 --> 00:02:08,960
it's a terrible strategy.

53
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,659
No, June choked out.

54
00:02:10,979 --> 00:02:13,000
She tasted something metallic in her mouth.

55
00:02:13,219 --> 00:02:13,419
Blood.

56
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:14,139
I'm bleeding.

57
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:14,819
Please.

58
00:02:15,379 --> 00:02:16,020
Stop acting.

59
00:02:16,379 --> 00:02:16,900
Cole snapped.

60
00:02:17,259 --> 00:02:20,219
She could almost see him adjusting his expensive cufflinks,

61
00:02:20,439 --> 00:02:21,680
annoyed by her existence.

62
00:02:22,199 --> 00:02:23,419
You are perfectly fine.

63
00:02:23,419 --> 00:02:25,599
We are walking on stage in two minutes.

64
00:02:26,039 --> 00:02:27,840
Do not call this number again tonight.

65
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:30,199
Cole, wait, the line went dead.

66
00:02:30,599 --> 00:02:32,639
The dial tone buzzed in the silent room.

67
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,479
It sounded like a death sentence.

68
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,560
June stared at the darkened screen.

69
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,800
Her phone slipped from her weak grasp, landing on the rug.

70
00:02:40,159 --> 00:02:43,259
A sudden, terrifying warmth spread between her thighs.

71
00:02:43,659 --> 00:02:44,379
June looked down.

72
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:48,759
A dark, thick pool of red was soaking into the intricate patterns of the Persian rug.

73
00:02:49,139 --> 00:02:49,340
Blood.

74
00:02:49,659 --> 00:02:50,439
So much blood.

75
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:52,719
A primal panic seized her chest.

76
00:02:52,719 --> 00:02:57,120
She was losing the baby with the last ounce of strength in her shaking fingers.

77
00:02:57,560 --> 00:03:00,000
She grabbed the phone again and dialed 911.

78
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:02,439
What is your emergency?

79
00:03:02,939 --> 00:03:03,719
Compton Manor.

80
00:03:03,979 --> 00:03:04,780
June whispered.

81
00:03:04,879 --> 00:03:06,599
Her voice barely leaving her throat.

82
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:07,360
Hemorrhaging.

83
00:03:07,599 --> 00:03:08,000
Pregnant.

84
00:03:08,259 --> 00:03:08,759
Please hurry.

85
00:03:09,259 --> 00:03:10,240
She dropped the phone.

86
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:12,400
Her head fell back against the floor.

87
00:03:12,759 --> 00:03:15,960
Across the room, the massive flat-screen TV was muted,

88
00:03:16,199 --> 00:03:18,539
playing a live broadcast of the charity gala.

89
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:21,300
Through her half-closed eyes, June saw Cole.

90
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:24,060
He looked breathtaking in his custom tuxedo.

91
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:24,939
He was smiling.

92
00:03:25,379 --> 00:03:29,259
He was smiling down at Alicia, who had her arm wrapped tightly around his.

93
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:32,500
Alicia wore a stunning white gown, looking like a bride.

94
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:37,020
Cole's eyes held a tenderness that June had not seen in four years of marriage.

95
00:03:37,419 --> 00:03:38,759
The contrast was brutal.

96
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:41,360
He was in the spotlight, holding another woman,

97
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,000
while his wife was bleeding out on his bedroom floor.

98
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:47,099
The whale of ambulance sirens pierced the night air,

99
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:47,979
growing louder.

100
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:50,939
Downstairs, the heavy oak doors banged open.

